  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Lars Seier Christensen is a Danish investor based in Switzerland who co-founded Saxo Bank and later established Seier Capital. His early business experience included a Spanish bar bought partly with an inheritance from his father. After learning brokerage in London, he built his fortune through banking and subsequently invested his own capital.",
    "html": "<p>Lars Seier Christensen is a Danish investor based in Switzerland who co-founded Saxo Bank and later established Seier Capital. His early business experience included a Spanish bar bought partly with an inheritance from his father. After learning brokerage in London, he built his fortune through banking and subsequently invested his own capital.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 52,
