  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Danish investor Lars Seier Christensen became a partner in Copenhagen’s Geranium after enjoying it as a diner. He bought into the restaurant alongside chef Rasmus Kofoed and director Søren Ledet. He valued the pleasure it gave guests and the goodwill created by entertaining business clients there.\n\nWhen Geranium first received three Michelin stars, its entire team celebrated at Tickets in Barcelona, with the restaurant reserved for the evening. Christensen also travelled on organised culinary trips to cities including San Sebastián and Lima. He valued the conversations and friendships formed around the table as well as the cooking.",
    "html": "<p>Danish investor Lars Seier Christensen became a partner in Copenhagen’s Geranium after enjoying it as a diner. He bought into the restaurant alongside chef Rasmus Kofoed and director Søren Ledet. He valued the pleasure it gave guests and the goodwill created by entertaining business clients there.</p>\r\n<p>When Geranium first received three Michelin stars, its entire team celebrated at Tickets in Barcelona, with the restaurant reserved for the evening. Christensen also travelled on organised culinary trips to cities including San Sebastián and Lima. He valued the conversations and friendships formed around the table as well as the cooking.</p>\r\n",
